/* The app's name, in the SYSTEM language. 2026-08-23, from the user:
   "app应该显示雅伟之言还是Yahweh's Words…要根据客户手机语言" — a fixed
   choice in either language reads as wrong to half the readers. iOS has
   followed that ruling since; macOS did not, so a Chinese-language Mac
   called it "Yahweh's Words" while the same person's Mi Pad called it
   雅伟之言.

   Two keys, because macOS reads two:
     CFBundleDisplayName — Finder, the Dock, Spotlight
     CFBundleName        — the bold menu-bar item next to
   Localizing only the first leaves the menu bar in English. */
"CFBundleDisplayName" = "Yahweh's Words";
"CFBundleName" = "Yahweh's Words";
